{
  "title": "Spinal Epidural Abscess",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/spine/2026/spinal-epidural-abscess",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jul 12 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Spinal epidural abscess is a spinal infection caused by a collection of pus or inflammatory granulation tissue between the dura mater and surrounding adipose tissue",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Early diagnosis is critical and is made with contrast-enhanced MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually prompt surgical decompression and long-term IV antibiotics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually seen in adults >60 y/o",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually located dorsally in the thoracolumbar spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**IV drug abuse**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "immunodeficiency",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "malignancy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "HIV",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "immunosuppressive medications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "recent spinal procedure",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "origin",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hematogenous spread ~50%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "spread from discitis ~33%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathogens",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**Staph aureus** is most common (50-65%)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Gram-negative organisms, such as E. coli (18%)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Pseudomonas in patients with IV drug use",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Neurologic deficits",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "33% of patients with an epidural abscess have been found to have neurologic symptoms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "4-22% incidence of permanent paralysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be caused by direct compression or infarction of blood flow to the spinal cord",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often associated with **vertebral osteomyelitis and discitis** (spondylodiscitis)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "present in ~18% of patients with spondylodiscitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "systemic illness is typically more profound than in patients with vertebral osteomyelitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**fever is present in ~50%**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often severe and insidious in onset",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "occurs in 87%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "neurologic deficits present in ~33%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may present as a radiculopathy or a myelopathy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Labs",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "WBC",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mean leukocyte count is 22,000 cells/mm³",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "elevated in ~42%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "ESR",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "elevated in >90% of cases (mean 86.3%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CRP",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "elevated in 90% of cases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually normal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "poor sensitivity for detecting epidural abscess",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT myelogram",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "90% sensitivity, but invasive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI with gadolinium",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "imaging modality of choice for the diagnosis of spinal epidural abscess",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2026/images/cervical_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "shows the extent of the abscess, presence of vertebral osteomyelitis, and degree of neurologic compression",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2026/images/170ej01[1]_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "gadolinium allows differentiation of pus from CSF",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2026/images/170ej02[1]_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "a **ring-enhancing lesion is pathognomonic** for an abscess",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "MRI of the entire spine should be performed to rule out skip epidural abscesses",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "concomitant infection outside the spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "delayed presentation (>7 days of symptoms)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ESR >95 mm/hour",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "bracing and IV antibiotics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "small abscess with minimal compression of neural elements and",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "no neurologic deficits and",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "patient capable of close clinical follow-up",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patients who are not candidates for surgery due to medical comorbidities",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "historically, the presence of an epidural abscess was considered a surgical emergency",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "recent trend toward nonoperative management, as new studies demonstrate that nonoperative treatment may be effective in patients without neurologic deficits",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "medical treatment failure is associated with:",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "neurologic deficits (strongest predictor of medical treatment failure)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "diabetes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "CRP >115 mg/L",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "WBC >12 k/mL",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "positive blood cultures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ">65 y/o",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "MRSA",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical decompression +/- spinal stabilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**neurologic deficits present**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "risk factors for failure of nonoperative management: older (>65 y/o), diabetics, new-onset neurologic deficits, and MRSA infection",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "evidence of spinal cord compression on imaging studies",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "persistent infection despite antibiotic therapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "progressive deformity or gross spinal instability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "postoperative antibiotics",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "2-4 weeks if no bony involvement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "6 weeks if bony involvement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Decompressive laminectomy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common form of operative treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "abscess is located posteriorly and there is no contiguous spondylodiscitis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "avoid wide decompression and facetectomy, as these can result in spinal instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Anterior debridement and strut grafting**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "abscess is located anteriorly",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anterior vertebral body and discs are involved (presence of spondylodiscitis)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Preoperative degree of neurologic deficit is the most important indicator of clinical outcome",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Mortality ~5%",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Early diagnosis is the most essential factor in preventing devastating complications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
